* soft-start-loop-gain -- the DC hand-over transfer of the FB-injection
* element: what current it actually delivers into FB as a function of the
* ramp node SSR, and what that does to the loop's operating point (issue #196).
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Why this deck exists next to tb_ss_loop_gain.spice.in
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* A phase margin is a statement about ONE operating point. tb_ss_loop_gain
* measures margins at a handful of pinned ramp states; this deck measures the
* operating point itself, densely, all the way along the ramp, so the margins
* have a curve to sit on rather than four isolated points.
*
* It is the SAME circuit, the SAME loop break (ERRAMP_OUT -> PASS_GATE with
* Vinj a DC short, so the DC solve is the true closed-loop one), the SAME
* resistive 36 ohm load model as the `ramp` phase, and the SAME SSR-port
* instrumented netlists. That is deliberate: at every V(SSR) the two decks
* share, they must land on the same DC operating point, and sweep.py checks
* exactly that before the transfer is allowed into the record.
*
* The sweep is a `foreach` over an explicit list of V(SSR) with an `op` at
* each, not a `.dc` analysis, for one reason: `op` is the analysis the margin
* deck uses, so a HOV line here and a ROW line there are the same computation
* at the same point and are directly comparable. Ops are milliseconds; the
* density costs nothing.
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* What is reported, and why each field
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*   fb_v      The feedback node. The soft-start mechanism is "hold FB at VREF
*             with an injected current and let the divider set VOUT", so
*             FB == VREF is the signature of the loop being IN REGULATION at
*             this ramp state, and FB above VREF means the injection element
*             is delivering more current than the divider can absorb with the
*             output at zero -- i.e. the loop is SATURATED, the error amp is
*             railed and the pass device is off. That state has no loop gain
*             and therefore no phase margin, which is precisely why it has to
*             be found here and not there.
*   vout_v    With FB at VREF the divider gives VOUT, and I_inj follows by KCL
*             (see sweep.py's Row.iinj_a -- the identical expression for both
*             DUT variants, so the A/B is like for like).
*   pg_v      The pass gate. Its distance from VIN is the direct, non-inferred
*             statement of whether the pass device is on at this ramp state.
*   erramp_v  The error amplifier's output, i.e. the far side of the loop
*             break. It equals pg_v at DC (Vinj is a 0 V source) and is
*             reported so a reader can see the break is a short, not a gap.
*   isup_a    Supply current, the same quantity every other bench here reports.
*   gmsum_v   ONLY for the device-level variant: the mirror node
*             Mgmr_ss/Mgmo_ss share as a gate. VIN - V(GMSUM) is Mgmo_ss's
*             source-gate drive, so this column is what says whether the
*             element has actually turned off or has merely gone weak. The
*             pre-#195 ideal-source variant has no such node and does not
*             emit the field.
*
* Template: the at-sign-delimited placeholders are substituted by sweep.py.

.include "@DESIGN_INCLUDE@"
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MOS_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @RES_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @BJT_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @DIODE_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MOSCAP_CORNER@
.lib "@MODEL_LIB@" @MIMCAP_CORNER@

.temp @TEMP_C@

* Per-finger model binning -- see tb_ss_loop_gain.spice.in's header and the
* README's "Model binning" section. Without this the deck does not parse.
.options wnflag=1

.include "@LDO_NETLIST@"

* --- stimulus ------------------------------------------------------------
Vin VIN 0 DC @VIN_V@
Ven EN 0 DC @VIN_V@
Vref VREF 0 DC 1.2

* --- DUT, loop broken at ERRAMP_OUT -> PASS_GATE (Vinj is a DC short) -----
Xdut VIN VOUT EN 0 AINJ BINJ VREF SSRPIN ldo_core
Vinj AINJ BINJ DC 0 AC 0

* --- the ramp node, pinned and swept -------------------------------------
Vssr SSRPIN 0 DC 0

* --- load + output network: the `ramp` phase's model ---------------------
* Resistive, because low on the ramp the regulated output is a fraction of a
* volt and an ideal sink demanding 50 mA from it has no solution on the
* regulating branch at all. 36 ohm is 1.8 V / 50 mA.
Rload VOUT NLD 36.0
Vlmeas NLD 0 DC 0
Resr VOUT NESR 0.001
Cout NESR 0 1e-6

* Same non-physical-DC-branch clamp as every other deck here; reverse-biased
* at the operating point and carries no AC (cjo=0 tt=0). There is no AC
* analysis in this deck at all.
.model dclamp d(is=1e-14 cjo=0 tt=0 n=1 rs=0)
Dclamp 0 VOUT dclamp

.control
set noaskquit

echo "* corner_id=@CORNER_ID@ corner=@CORNER_NAME@ temp_c=@TEMP_C@ vin_v=@VIN_V@"
echo "* variant=@VARIANT@ analysis=dc-handover-transfer load=resistive-36ohm"
echo "* columns: HOV ssr_cmd= ssr_v= fb_v= vout_v= pg_v= erramp_v= isup_a=@GMSUM_COL@"
echo "* (I_inj into FB is DERIVED from fb_v/vout_v by KCL in sweep.py, not"
echo "*  measured, so the identical expression reads both DUT variants;"
echo "*  fb_v away from VREF means the loop is not in regulation at that ramp"
echo "*  state and neither VOUT nor I_inj is a regulating-branch quantity)"
echo "* Fields are key=value for the same reason the margin deck's are: an"
echo "* empty positional field vanishes into the whitespace."

foreach ss @SSR_LIST@
  destroy all
  alter Vssr dc = $ss
  op
  let fb_dc = v(xdut.fb)
  let vout_dc = v(vout)
  let pg_dc = v(binj)
  let ea_dc = v(ainj)
  let isup_dc = -i(vin)
  let ssr_dc = v(ssrpin)
@GMSUM_LET@
  echo "HOV ssr_cmd=$ss ssr_v=$&ssr_dc fb_v=$&fb_dc vout_v=$&vout_dc pg_v=$&pg_dc erramp_v=$&ea_dc isup_a=$&isup_dc@GMSUM_ECHO@"
end
echo "* SWEEP COMPLETE @CORNER_ID@"
.endc
.end
